 ### New features
 
-- The Telsiz DJ player can be moved: when the DJ card is not visible, the player in the corner of the screen can be dragged by its bar and dropped in one of the four corners, the Move button goes through the corners in turn, and the chosen corner is stored on the device. Between 760 and 1279 pixels the player sits at the top right below the band by default, and in a bottom corner it moves above the message box and the radio card as long as there is room, so it does not cover the voice buttons. Minimize leaves only the bar: an audio file keeps playing, and a YouTube track pauses on that device only and resumes in sync with the room with Show. The Floating Player switch keeps the player in the corner even while the card is visible, and an audio file then also shows in the corner with its waveform and bar. The name of the playing track and "Telsiz DJ · room" are given to your system's media controls and lock screen (Media Session), which can be turned off in the Media controls section of Settings > Privacy. Play and Pause there only affect that device and do not stop the room's music. When someone else adds a track to Telsiz DJ in your voice room, a line with the track's name appears in the Notifications list.
+- The Telsiz DJ player can be moved: when the DJ card is not visible, the player in the corner of the screen can be dragged by its bar and dropped in one of the four corners, the Move button goes through the corners in turn, and the chosen corner is stored on the device. The default corner is the first one that does not cover the buttons of the radio card, the message box or the Room info button in the conversation header (between 760 and 1279 pixels the top right comes first, below the band and the conversation header). In a bottom corner the player moves above the message box and the radio card as long as there is room, as long as there is room it does not come down onto the card's buttons in any corner, and it stays inside the viewport in a short window too. While a layer that covers the main view, such as Settings, is open, the player sits in the bottom corner of the chosen side, and every row of Settings can be reached by scrolling. Minimize leaves only the bar: an audio file keeps playing, and a YouTube track pauses on that device only and resumes in sync with the room with Show. The Floating Player switch keeps the player in the corner even while the card is visible, and an audio file then also shows in the corner with its waveform and bar. The name of the playing track and "Telsiz DJ · room" are given to your system's media controls and lock screen (Media Session), which can be turned off in the Media controls section of Settings > Privacy. Play and Pause there only affect that device and do not stop the room's music, and that pause is lifted when you leave the voice room. When someone else adds a track to Telsiz DJ in your voice room, a line with the track's name appears in the Notifications list, and these lines do not push the line of an ongoing screen share with its Watch button out of the list.
 
 ### Changes
 
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ Notable changes in Telsiz releases are listed in this file. Version numbers foll
 
 ### Fixes
 
-- Telsiz DJ: the first YouTube track added while the tab was in the background (or the desktop window was minimized) never started on that device and started in the middle once the page came to the front. The card is now drawn on a hidden page too, and the track starts together with the other devices. The announcement in the text room did not show the track's name ("added a YouTube track"), and now it goes out with the name: the name is awaited for up to 8 seconds, if it arrives later the announcement of the person who added it is edited with the name, and the edited label is not shown. A file added with "Play in DJ" was never announced, and now it is announced with its name in the text room where the file is. The last action line on the DJ card also reads the name from the queue. In windows narrower than 1280 pixels the player in the corner covered the voice buttons of the radio card.
+- Telsiz DJ: the first YouTube track added while the tab was in the background (or the desktop window was minimized) never started on that device and started in the middle once the page came to the front. The card is now drawn on a hidden page too, and the track starts together with the other devices. The announcement in the text room did not show the track's name ("added a YouTube track"), and now it goes out with the name: the name is awaited for up to 8 seconds (if the page is hidden or closed in the meantime the announcement goes out at once without it), if it arrives later the announcement of the person who added it is edited with the name, and the edited label is not shown for that edit. An edit made more than 10 minutes after the announcement was sent (with one minute allowed for delay) shows the label. A file added with "Play in DJ" was never announced, and now it is announced with its name in the text room where the file is. The last action line on the DJ card also reads the name from the queue. In windows narrower than 1280 pixels the player in the corner covered the voice buttons of the radio card.
 - In the Arcade and Turquoise and Copper themes the border of the camera indicator on the radio card ("Your camera is on, everyone in the room can see it") and of the notice shown when someone starts sharing their screen was not drawn at all. The muted Microphone and active Camera buttons of a direct message call, the chip and panel of your own share, the Stop Watching button, the Telsiz DJ error box and the verified safety number button were also drawn in the text color instead of their own border color. Both themes now have live and danger border colors, and the borders show with at least 3:1 contrast on every surface.
 
